sample: 200 office parcels, 200 mf parcels of 1186 built

=== THE CITY'S VACANCY vs THE BUILDINGS' VACANCY ===
  office       citywide vac mean 0.141 (range 0.037..0.301)
               PARCEL   vac mean 0.123 (range 0.097..0.255)
               corr = 0.086   slope d(parcelVac)/d(cityVac) = 0.042   <-- 1.0 would mean the buildings track the city
  multifamily  citywide vac mean 0.072 (range 0.013..0.241)
               PARCEL   vac mean 0.047 (range 0.038..0.099)
               corr = 0.075   slope d(parcelVac)/d(cityVac) = 0.017   <-- 1.0 would mean the buildings track the city

=== IS THE VACANCY->CAP TERM SATURATED? ===
  office vacRisk: mean 0.322  at +2.0 ceiling 0.8% of months  at -0.6 floor 5.1% of months

=== THE CONSTRUCTION CYCLE ===
  office vac autocorr crosses zero at 36m, returns positive at 99m => period ~144m (12.0 yr)
  office spells above natural vacancy: median 71m, p90 116m, longest 135m (n=31)
  at local peaks of office starts (n=55): vac now 0.121, vac +36m 0.164, vac +60m 0.152 (natural 0.115)
  seed: office stock 5.00M -> 12.60M sf (+152% over 75y), employment x2.41
  seed: office stock 5.00M -> 11.84M sf (+137% over 75y), employment x2.54
  seed: office stock 5.00M -> 12.23M sf (+144% over 75y), employment x2.42
  seed: office stock 5.00M -> 12.74M sf (+155% over 75y), employment x2.48

=== LAND: WHAT DOES IT ACTUALLY RESPOND TO? ===
  corr(log landIdx, log office rent) = 0.936
  corr(log landIdx, index rate)      = 0.186
  corr(log landIdx, credit)          = -0.049
  corr(log landIdx, office cap)      = 0.316
  corr(log landIdx, cost idx)        = 0.944
  corr(log landIdx, office vac)      = 0.347
  corr(log landIdx, log(rent/cap) - log cost) = 0.015   <-- the residual-value theory of land

=== DOES LAND PRICE GATE CONSTRUCTION? ===
  corr(log(landIdx/costIdx), office starts/stock) = 0.041   (real: strongly NEGATIVE)
